# Silvain Aster's personal quest, Aurel's Last Chapter (data/quests/aurels_last_chapter.json,
# docs/story/personal_quests.md). Every scene needs Silvain: when a custom hero takes their place the quest never
# starts. Started from into_the_mists/arrival:hooks. The satchel and the cipher: the camp talk after Aurel's note is
# read (camp/silvain). The hunter: Rictavio, below. The margins: the Amber Temple library (prop aurel_margins). Still
# reading: the camp talk once the Tome is found. The last page is the castle's east tower (Phase 6 hook).

# --- Rictavio remembers (vallaki/rictavio:menu) -------------------------------------------------------------------

~ rictavio
set aurel_rictavio_told
interject name:silvain_aster: A scholar came through Vallaki a year ago. Thin, ink to the elbows, a list of questions about one book. Aurel Mirescu. Did he talk to you?
Rictavio [weary]: ...Mirescu. Yes. He sat on the steps of my wagon and asked me, very politely, whether I believed a certain lord had written his own history. I asked who wanted to know. He said, "Everyone who's read the index."
Rictavio: I told him to go home. I told him some books are written to be read, the way some doors are built to be opened, and he should ask himself who was holding the handle.
interject name:silvain_aster: And?
Rictavio [sad]: He thanked me, beautifully. Then he asked the way to the mountains, because the index was kept in a temple of amber and he wanted to see the shape of the thing before he read it.
Rictavio: If he was your friend, I'm sorry. He was the bravest coward I've ever met. Shaking the whole time, and asking his questions anyway.
interject name:silvain_aster: That's my line. I've been using it for a year. It's a good line. ...Thank you.
if not (quest.aurels_last_chapter >= the_hunter)
quest aurels_last_chapter the_hunter
endif
if flag.rictavio_unmasked
-> vallaki/rictavio:hunter_menu
endif
-> vallaki/rictavio:menu

# --- The Amber Temple library: a note in the margins (prop aurel_margins) ---------------------------------------

~ margins
if flag.aurel_margins_found
Narrator: The note is still in the margin in faded brown ink. Silvain reads it again anyway, lips moving.
-> END
endif
set aurel_margins_found
Narrator: Among the chained books one has been read in the last year: the dust on its spine is thinner, and a strip of good paper marks a page near the end. The margins are crowded with a small, fast, educated hand.
interject name:silvain_aster: Sevens crossed. That's Aurel. He writes in library books. I have told him a hundred times. Give me a moment.
Narrator: The note is addressed, in the shorthand the two of them invented to pass notes in lectures, to "S." Silvain reads it aloud as if every word costs a coin.
interject name:silvain_aster: "S. If you have followed me here, you are an idiot, and I'm glad. The book is real. He wrote it to be read. That is the thing nobody understands."
interject name:silvain_aster: "He doesn't want blood half as much as he wants an audience. Three hundred years and no one to tell. I'm going up to be the audience. I think I can keep him talking until I find the ending. Bring a lamp. A."
interject name:silvain_aster: ...Idiot. Brave, footnoted idiot.
if flag.visitors_ledger_read
interject name:silvain_aster: And he signed their ledger, under the prince's entry. "A. Mirescu, a reader. Admitted." Of course he did.
endif
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: He left you a note in a library book. In code. That's the most romantic thing I've ever seen, and I've seen a man propose with a stolen horse.
interject name:silvain_aster: It is not romantic. It is correct citation practice. Be quiet.
if not (quest.aurels_last_chapter >= the_margins)
quest aurels_last_chapter the_margins
endif
-> END
